IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-insurable-employment`
IMPORT `er2-common`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 29 to 32: when a claimant is considered to have worked a full working week
-- (special cases, the self-employed, everyone else), the week of unemployment of a self-employed person, and the working day.
-- Piece er2 (Sonnet 5.5), LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Every src:N is a line of SOR-96-332.txt, an unofficial plain-text rendering; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- A week is Sunday to Saturday (s 2(1) "week") and is named by any day in it. Where the text hands a judgment to someone ("such a minor extent
-- that a person would not normally rely on ...") the judgment is a BOOLEAN input named for it, never computed (phrasebook 8.1).
-- The text does not say how regulations 29, 30 and 31 are to be read together when more than one could apply; section 31 says it is for a
-- claimant "other than a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30", and section 29(2) says "notwithstanding section 31" (fork F10).

§ `Regulation 29 - Employed person working a full working week: special cases`

§§ `Regulation 29(1) - a railway employee remunerated on a mileage basis`

-- src:462 | 29 (1) A claimant is considered to have worked a full working week during each week in the two-week period reported on in the declaration filed when making a claim for benefits where the claimant
-- src:463 | (a) is a railway employee;
-- src:464 | (b) is remunerated on a mileage basis; and
-- src:465 | (c) is remunerated in that two-week period at not less than twice the maximum weekly insurable earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 29(1) (src:462-465)
GIVEN `the claimant is a railway employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is remunerated on a mileage basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's remuneration in the two-week period reported on in the declaration` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: the maximum weekly insurable earnings is section 14(1.1) of the Act (piece ei1)
DECIDE `reg 29(1) the claimant is considered to have worked a full working week during each week in the two-week period` IF
        `the claimant is a railway employee`
    AND `the claimant is remunerated on a mileage basis`
    AND `the claimant's remuneration in the two-week period reported on in the declaration` AT LEAST (2 TIMES `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`)

§§ `Regulation 29(2) - farming or horticulture`

-- src:466 | (2) Notwithstanding section 31, a claimant who is employed in farming or horticulture is considered to have worked a full working week during any week in which the claimant works
-- src:467 | (a) not less than five days; and
-- src:468 | (b) not less than 35 hours in total.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 29(2) (src:466-468)
GIVEN `the claimant is employed in farming or horticulture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the claimant works in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of hours the claimant works in the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- "Notwithstanding section 31": this paragraph prevails over section 31 for the claimants it describes.
DECIDE `reg 29(2) the claimant employed in farming or horticulture is considered to have worked a full working week` IF
        `the claimant is employed in farming or horticulture`
    AND `the number of days the claimant works in the week` AT LEAST 5
    AND `the total number of hours the claimant works in the week` AT LEAST 35

§§ `Regulation 29(3) - a holiday in the week`

-- src:469 | (3) Where, in any week, a claimant does not work on a holiday or, by reason of a holiday, does not work on the working day that immediately precedes or immediately follows that holiday, the claimant shall be regarded as having worked a full working week if, on each of the remaining working days in that week, the claimant works a number of hours at least equal to the number that the claimant would normally work.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 29(3) (src:469)
GIVEN `the claimant does not work on a holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of a holiday, the claimant does not work on the working day that immediately precedes or immediately follows that holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the remaining working days in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those remaining working days on which the claimant works at least the number of hours the claimant would normally work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 29(3) the claimant is regarded as having worked a full working week despite a holiday` IF
        (   `the claimant does not work on a holiday`
         OR `by reason of a holiday, the claimant does not work on the working day that immediately precedes or immediately follows that holiday`)
    AND `the number of those remaining working days on which the claimant works at least the number of hours the claimant would normally work` EQUALS `the number of the remaining working days in the week`

§§ `Regulation 29(4) - remuneration payable for a period longer than a week`

-- src:470 | (4) Where an insured person is employed under a contract of employment under which the usual remuneration is payable in respect of a period greater than a week, regardless of the amount of work performed in the period, each week that falls wholly in that period is a full working week for the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 29(4) (src:470)
GIVEN `the usual remuneration is payable under the contract of employment in respect of the period, regardless of the amount of work performed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period in respect of which the usual remuneration is payable` IS A `Period of days`
      `a day in the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 29(4) the week is a full working week for the insured person` IF
        `the usual remuneration is payable under the contract of employment in respect of the period, regardless of the amount of work performed in it`
    AND `the number of days in` `the period in respect of which the usual remuneration is payable` GREATER THAN 7
    AND `er2 a period lies wholly within another` (`er2 the week containing the day` `a day in the week`) `the period in respect of which the usual remuneration is payable`

§ `Regulation 30 - Self-employed person working a full working week`

§§ `Regulation 30(5) - self-employed person, for the purposes of this regulation`

-- src:485 | (5) For the purposes of this section, self-employed person means an individual who
-- src:486 | (a) is or was engaged in a business; or
-- src:487 | (b) is employed but does not have insurable employment by reason of paragraph 5(2)(b) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(5) (src:485-487)
GIVEN `the individual is or was engaged in a business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion of the voting shares of the corporation that the individual controls` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- (b): "employed but does not have insurable employment by reason of paragraph 5(2)(b) of the Act", that is, the employment is excluded because
-- the person controls more than 40% of the voting shares of the corporation that employs them (the keel's `s 5(2)(b) ...`).
DECIDE `reg 30(5) self-employed person` IF
        `the individual is or was engaged in a business`
    OR  (    `the individual is employed`
         AND `s 5(2)(b) employment of a person by a corporation they control` `the employer is a corporation` `the portion of the voting shares of the corporation that the individual controls`)

§§ `Regulation 30(1) - what is considered a full working week`

-- src:473 | 30 (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (4), where during any week a claimant is self-employed or engaged in the operation of a business on the claimant's own account or in a partnership or co-adventure, or is employed in any other employment in which the claimant controls their working hours, the claimant is considered to have worked a full working week during that week.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(1) (src:473)
GIVEN `the claimant is a self-employed person within subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is engaged in the operation of a business on the claimant's own account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is engaged in the operation of a business in a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is engaged in the operation of a business in a co-adventure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is employed in any other employment in which the claimant controls their working hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 30(1) the claimant's work in the week is of a kind that is considered a full working week, before subsections (2) and (4)` IF
        (   `the claimant is a self-employed person within subsection (5)`
         OR `the claimant is engaged in the operation of a business on the claimant's own account`
         OR `the claimant is engaged in the operation of a business in a partnership`
         OR `the claimant is engaged in the operation of a business in a co-adventure`)
    OR  `the claimant is employed in any other employment in which the claimant controls their working hours`

§§ `Regulation 30(2), (3) - a minor extent`

-- src:474 | (2) Where a claimant is employed or engaged in the operation of a business as described in subsection (1) to such a minor extent that a person would not normally rely on that employment or engagement as a principal means of livelihood, the claimant is, in respect of that employment or engagement, not regarded as working a full working week.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(2) (src:474)
GIVEN `the work in the week is of a kind described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment or engagement is to such a minor extent that a person would not normally rely on it as a principal means of livelihood` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- The standard is a judgment of whoever decides the claim, informed by the circumstances of subsection (3); it is an input, not a computation.
DECIDE `reg 30(2) the claimant is not regarded as working a full working week in respect of that employment or engagement` IF
        `the work in the week is of a kind described in subsection (1)`
    AND `the employment or engagement is to such a minor extent that a person would not normally rely on it as a principal means of livelihood`

-- src:475 | (3) The circumstances to be considered in determining whether the claimant's employment or engagement in the operation of a business is of the minor extent described in subsection (2) are
-- src:476 | (a) the time spent;
-- src:477 | (b) the nature and amount of the capital and resources invested;
-- src:478 | (c) the financial success or failure of the employment or business;
-- src:479 | (d) the continuity of the employment or business;
-- src:480 | (e) the nature of the employment or business; and
-- src:481 | (f) the claimant's intention and willingness to seek and immediately accept alternate employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(3) (src:475-481)
DECLARE `er2 Circumstance considered in judging whether employment is of a minor extent` IS ONE OF
    `er2 the time spent`                                                                                   -- (a)
    `er2 the nature and amount of the capital and resources invested`                                      -- (b)
    `er2 the financial success or failure of the employment or business`                                   -- (c)
    `er2 the continuity of the employment or business`                                                     -- (d)
    `er2 the nature of the employment or business`                                                         -- (e)
    `er2 the claimant's intention and willingness to seek and immediately accept alternate employment`    -- (f)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(3) (src:475-481)
GIVETH A LIST OF `er2 Circumstance considered in judging whether employment is of a minor extent`
`reg 30(3) the circumstances to be considered in determining whether employment or engagement is of a minor extent` MEANS
    LIST `er2 the time spent`
       , `er2 the nature and amount of the capital and resources invested`
       , `er2 the financial success or failure of the employment or business`
       , `er2 the continuity of the employment or business`
       , `er2 the nature of the employment or business`
       , `er2 the claimant's intention and willingness to seek and immediately accept alternate employment`

§§ `Regulation 30(4) - farming from October to March`

-- The period begins with the week in which 1 October falls and ends with the week in which the following 31 March falls: whole weeks,
-- Sunday to Saturday. The argument is the year of the 1 October.
-- src:482 | (4) Where a claimant is employed in farming and subsection (2) does not apply to that employment, the claimant shall not be considered to have worked a full working week at any time during the period that begins with the week in which October 1st falls and ends with the week in which the following March 31 falls, if the claimant proves that during that period
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(4) (src:482)
GIVEN `the year in which October 1st falls` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `reg 30(4) the period that begins with the week in which October 1st falls and ends with the week in which the following March 31 falls` IS
    `Period of days` OF (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (YMD `the year in which October 1st falls` 10 1)), (`s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (YMD (`the year in which October 1st falls` PLUS 1) 3 31))

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(4) (src:482)
GIVEN `a day in the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 30(4) the week falls in the period from the week of October 1st to the week of the following March 31` IF
        `er2 a period lies wholly within another` (`er2 the week containing the day` `a day in the week`) (`reg 30(4) the period that begins with the week in which October 1st falls and ends with the week in which the following March 31 falls` (DATE_YEAR `a day in the week`))
    OR  `er2 a period lies wholly within another` (`er2 the week containing the day` `a day in the week`) (`reg 30(4) the period that begins with the week in which October 1st falls and ends with the week in which the following March 31 falls` ((DATE_YEAR `a day in the week`) MINUS 1))

-- src:483 | (a) the claimant did not work; or
-- src:484 | (b) the claimant was employed to such a minor extent that it would not have prevented the claimant from accepting full-time employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(4) (src:482-484)
GIVEN `the claimant is employed in farming` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) does not apply to that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the week` IS A DATE
      `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant did not work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant was employed to such a minor extent that it would not have prevented the claimant from accepting full-time employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 30(4) the claimant employed in farming is not considered to have worked a full working week in the week` IF
        `the claimant is employed in farming`
    AND `subsection (2) does not apply to that employment`
    AND `reg 30(4) the week falls in the period from the week of October 1st to the week of the following March 31` `a day in the week`
    AND (   `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant did not work`
         OR `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant was employed to such a minor extent that it would not have prevented the claimant from accepting full-time employment`)

§§ `Regulation 30 - the result for a week`

-- JUST TRUE: considered to have worked a full working week (subsection (1)); JUST FALSE: not regarded as, or not considered to have, worked
-- one ((2) or (4), which prevail over (1): "Subject to subsections (2) and (4)"); NOTHING: regulation 30 does not decide the week.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30(1), (2), (4) (src:473) (src:474) (src:482-484)
GIVEN `the work in the week is of a kind described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment or engagement is to such a minor extent that a person would not normally rely on it as a principal means of livelihood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is employed in farming` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the week` IS A DATE
      `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant did not work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant was employed to such a minor extent that it would not have prevented the claimant from accepting full-time employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 30 whether the claimant is considered to have worked a full working week in the week` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the work in the week is of a kind described in subsection (1)`)
           THEN NOTHING
           IF `reg 30(2) the claimant is not regarded as working a full working week in respect of that employment or engagement` `the work in the week is of a kind described in subsection (1)` `the employment or engagement is to such a minor extent that a person would not normally rely on it as a principal means of livelihood`
           THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `reg 30(4) the claimant employed in farming is not considered to have worked a full working week in the week` `the claimant is employed in farming` (NOT (`reg 30(2) the claimant is not regarded as working a full working week in respect of that employment or engagement` `the work in the week is of a kind described in subsection (1)` `the employment or engagement is to such a minor extent that a person would not normally rely on it as a principal means of livelihood`)) `a day in the week` `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant did not work` `the claimant proves that during that period the claimant was employed to such a minor extent that it would not have prevented the claimant from accepting full-time employment`
           THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Regulation 30.1 - Week of unemployment of a self-employed person`

-- src:490 | 30.1 For the purposes of Part VII.1 of the Act, a week of unemployment for a self-employed person is, despite section 30, a week in which the person reduces the time devoted to their business activities by more than 40% of the normal level.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30.1 (src:490)
GIVEN `the normal level of the time devoted to the business activities in a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the time devoted to the business activities in the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: Part VII.1 of the Act (piece ei5). The unit (hours, say) is the caller's; only the proportion matters.
DECIDE `reg 30.1 the week is a week of unemployment for a self-employed person` IF
    (`the normal level of the time devoted to the business activities in a week` MINUS `the time devoted to the business activities in the week`) GREATER THAN (40% TIMES `the normal level of the time devoted to the business activities in a week`)

§ `Regulation 30.2 - Self-employed person deemed to be not working`

-- src:491 | 30.2 For the purposes of subsection 152.03(4) of the Act, a self-employed person is deemed to be not working if they are not engaged in
-- src:492 | (a) the normal activities of their business; and
-- src:493 | (b) the normal activities for the continuation of their business.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 30.2 (src:491-493)
GIVEN `the self-employed person is engaged in the normal activities of their business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the self-employed person is engaged in the normal activities for the continuation of their business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: subsection 152.03(4) of the Act (piece ei5). "not engaged in (a) ...; and (b) ...": engaged in neither (fork F11 in NOTES.md).
DECIDE `reg 30.2 the self-employed person is deemed to be not working` IF
        (NOT (`the self-employed person is engaged in the normal activities of their business`))
    AND (NOT (`the self-employed person is engaged in the normal activities for the continuation of their business`))

§ `Regulation 31 - Employed persons working a full working week`

-- src:496 | 31 (1) A full working week of a claimant, other than a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30, is the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant is or was employed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 31(1) (src:496)
GIVEN `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- NOTHING: the regulation is for "a claimant, other than a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30".
DECIDE `reg 31(1) the number of hours, days or shifts in a full working week` IS
    IF   `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises`

-- src:497 | (2) When the number of hours, days or shifts referred to in subsection (1) is the number that is normally worked by persons in part-time employment and is less than the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons employed in full-time employment in the employment that is closest in nature to the claimant's employment, the claimant is considered to have worked a full working week when the claimant has worked the number of hours, days or shifts that are normally worked by a person in full-time employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 31(2) (src:497)
GIVEN `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises` IS A NUMBER
      `that number is the number normally worked by persons in part-time employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons employed in full-time employment in the employment that is closest in nature to the claimant's employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- When the part-time number is less than the full-time number, the claimant has worked a full working week on working the full-time number.
DECIDE `reg 31(2) the number of hours, days or shifts that makes a full working week for a part-time claimant` IS
    IF   `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   `that number is the number normally worked by persons in part-time employment`
              AND `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises` LESS THAN `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons employed in full-time employment in the employment that is closest in nature to the claimant's employment`
         THEN JUST `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons employed in full-time employment in the employment that is closest in nature to the claimant's employment`
         ELSE JUST `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises`

-- src:498 | (3) The full working week of a claimant, other than a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30, who is remunerated on a piece, mileage or other unit rate is the number of days normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant is or was employed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 31(3) (src:498)
GIVEN `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 31(3) the number of days in a full working week for a claimant remunerated on a piece, mileage or other unit rate` IS
    IF   `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the number of days normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises`

-- Which of (1), (2) and (3) gives the number: (3) for a claimant remunerated on a piece, mileage or other unit rate, otherwise (1) as
-- adjusted by (2) (for a claimant who is not part-time, (2) gives the number of (1)). NOTHING for a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 31(1), (2), (3) (src:496) (src:497) (src:498)
GIVEN `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is remunerated on a piece, mileage or other unit rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises` IS A NUMBER
      `that number is the number normally worked by persons in part-time employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons employed in full-time employment in the employment that is closest in nature to the claimant's employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 31 the number of hours, days or shifts that makes a full working week for the claimant` IS
    IF   `the claimant is remunerated on a piece, mileage or other unit rate`
    THEN `reg 31(3) the number of days in a full working week for a claimant remunerated on a piece, mileage or other unit rate` `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30` `the number of days normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises`
    ELSE `reg 31(2) the number of hours, days or shifts that makes a full working week for a part-time claimant` `the claimant is a claimant referred to in section 29 or 30` `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons in the claimant's grade, class or shift at the factory, workshop or other premises` `that number is the number normally worked by persons in part-time employment` `the number of hours, days or shifts normally worked in a calendar week by persons employed in full-time employment in the employment that is closest in nature to the claimant's employment`

-- "has worked": at least the number (fork F12 in NOTES.md). NOTHING when regulation 31 gives no number for the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 31(1), (2), (3) (src:496) (src:497) (src:498)
GIVEN `the number of hours, days or shifts the claimant worked in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the number that makes a full working week for the claimant` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 31 the claimant has worked a full working week` IS
    CONSIDER `the number that makes a full working week for the claimant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST required THEN JUST (`the number of hours, days or shifts the claimant worked in the week` AT LEAST required)

§ `Regulation 32 - Working day`

-- src:501 | 32 For the purposes of sections 18 and 152.19 of the Act, a working day is any day of the week except Saturday and Sunday.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 32 (src:501)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: sections 18 and 152.19 of the Act (pieces ei1, ei5). Public holidays are working days here: only Saturday and Sunday are excluded.
DECIDE `reg 32 working day` IF
    `is weekday` d
